# Defect classes this project ships

`/operate` checks every diff against each class that applies, and the review rounds use the list as a checklist.
The kit seeds it with classes that recur across stacks. Add your own as reviews find them, one line each, in the
same shape: the defect, then what to check. Put the ticket key in brackets at the end if you want the trail.
Remove a seeded class only if it truly can't occur in this stack.

## Normalization and validation

- A comparison whose two sides normalize differently. Check: both sides go through the same helper.
- A value stored raw while its normalized form is what decides. Check: store the value in the form it is compared in.
- A request field the handler reads but the input validator never declares, so validation strips it. Check: every
  field read is declared.
- New branch logic on a nullable source field, with only the happy path traced. Check: trace the null and missing
  cases.

## Siblings and entry points

- One of N sibling call sites left on the old pattern. Check: grep for every site and `docs/agent/sibling-paths.md`.
- A guard on one input path while its siblings reach the same downstream unguarded. Check: list every path into that
  downstream.
- A guard that reads a verdict only some producers write. Check: list every producer of the verdict.

## Error handling and lifecycle

- A handler that logs a query error and continues with partial data. Check: every error throws.
- Cleanup that runs on every exit, including the ones that must not clean up. Check: walk each exit path.
- An `await` inserted into a synchronous batch, splitting the flush. Check: the batch still applies as one.
- A gate whose value is decided before the finding it depends on exists. Check: the order in which the inputs are
  produced.

## Counting, scanning and parsing

- A count taken from the length of a display-limited list. Check: counts come from a count query or a stored counter.
- A scan that reads the whole file or input when it meant one construct. Check: the scan is bounded to that construct.
- A region located by character distance instead of structure. Check: locate it by parsing.
- A pattern applied to raw text, so string contents and comments read as code. Check: match on structure, or strip
  strings and comments first.
- An unbounded pattern over input an operator or user controls. Check: bound it and measure it on a large input.

## UI state

- An async action that fires while its validation request is still in flight, or a nonce-guarded `.finally()` that
  isn't gated. Check: the pending state disables the action, and `.finally()` checks the nonce.

## Tests and CI

- A mocked call that cannot prove what happens on the other side of it. Check: something real covers that side.
- Mock state leaking between tests: a reset that doesn't clear return values, or queued one-shot values left over.
  Check: each test sets up its own mocks.
- A test that passes vacuously. Check: mutation-test it; break the code and watch it go red.
- A green CI run that is really a skip, hiding breakage. Check: the job ran and executed tests.
- An unpinned third-party install that changes behaviour with no change in the repo. Check: versions are pinned.

